1b:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose-custom max-w-none","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Choosing between DigitalOcean, Linode, and Vultr in 2026 is one of the most common dilemmas for developers, startups, and SMBs. All three offer simple pricing, solid performance, and developer-friendly interfaces—but the differences in global coverage, compute options, managed services, and ecosystem maturity can significantly impact your workflow and bottom line."]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["I’ve spent the past two weeks benchmarking instances across all three platforms, analyzing pricing models, comparing network performance from global vantage points, and aggregating verified G2 user reviews. Here’s the definitive 2026 comparison."]}],["$","h2","4",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#F0F2FE] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"Market Overview"}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["As of Q1 2026, the “SMB cloud trio” collectively serves over 4 million developers worldwide. DigitalOcean leads in brand recognition and community engagement with 1.5M+ developers and the most popular community tutorial platform. Linode (Akamai-backed) leads in raw compute performance and enterprise security posture. Vultr leads in geographic coverage with 32+ data centers versus 15 for DigitalOcean and 16 for Linode."]}],["$","h2","8",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#F0F2FE] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"Pricing Comparison"}],["$","p","10",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["All three providers use transparent flat-rate pricing, but the details matter:"]}],["$","div","table-21",{"className":"overflow-x-auto mb-6","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-sm border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",n